The  driver supports the Intel i31244 Serial ATA and controllers,
and provides the interface with the hardware for the driver.  The
0x0002 flag forces the driver to  disable  DMA  on  chipsets  for
which  DMA  would normally be enabled.  This can be used as a de‐
bugging aid, or to work around problems where the SATA controller
is wired up to the system incorrectly.  Early samples of the  In‐
tel  i31244  Serial ATA controller revision 0 had a bug affecting
DMA data transfers.  Full production samples have been fixed, but
have the same revision number.  The option can be used to disable
DMA on the buggy revisions.
